# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=whisper spec=warrior:arms style=melee
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=844x390,touch save=fresh
#
# boss=whisper is a coverage label only -- a mode=walk evening steers at no
# named boss, the walk starts at the door same as any other. From a fresh
# door, "whisper" (The Last Whisper) sits in oratory, the fifth room:
# threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow) -> climb -> oratory(whisper).
#
# What no session has done before: grepped sessions.jsonl for every prior
# melee-style walk/clear -- rogue:assassination (moveSpeed 178, clean),
# shaman:elemental x2 (167, clean), warlock:destruction (158, wiped),
# priest:discipline x2 (158, wiped), priest:shadow (158, wiped 9/9).
# warrior:arms has never been run under melee at all, on any mode. Its own
# moveSpeed is 158 (src/sim/classes.ts:444) -- the same tier as every prior
# wipe and distinct from every prior clean crossing -- so this is a third
# class at the losing side of direction.md hypothesis 6's class-speed
# threshold, a stronger confirmation than a second if it also wipes, and a
# genuine overturn of the threshold if it instead crosses clean.
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:warrior:arms
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets

# Chunk 1: threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow) -> climb -> oratory(whisper).
# Evening stops itself early (evening-stuck) if two rooms in a row go
# nowhere; budget kept inside one foreground invocation.
evening melee 200 6
shot after-evening-1
state
says
bill
targets
